I remain confident in **25 and 74**. Current round split is roughly 8 for **25/74** and 6 for **4/11**.

Core evidence for **25/74**: the double sestina’s end-words are *mountains, valleys, forests, music, morning, evening*. The closing envoi at 73–75 should gather these in pairs: 73 has *mountains/valleys*, 75 has *morning/evening*, so 74 must supply *forests/music*. Line 25, “These forests eke, made wretched by our music,” supplies exactly that missing pair. Swapping 25 and 74 restores:
73 mountains/valleys;
74 forests/music;
75 morning/evening.

It also repairs 25–26 grammar: after the swap, line 25 becomes “Long since, alas, my deadly swannish music,” whose singular *music* naturally anticipates “Hath made itself…” in 26. In the current text, “These forests … Hath made itself” is discordant. My memory of the known Sidney text also supports line 25 being the “Long since…” line and the envoi line being “These forests eke…”

Rival **4/11** remains the main alternative. Colleagues 1, 5, 7, 9, 13, and 14 argue that lines 4 and 11 are near-identical invocation lines in corresponding slots, both ending in *music*, and the “your/you” asymmetry is the concrete residue of a swap. Colleague 5 adds that “Vouchsafe you” may be an archaic imperative with expressed subject, and that the pronoun distribution may be reversed between Strephon and Klaius.

Rebuttal: 4/11 does not repair the envoi or the 25–26 grammatical break. Swapping 4/11 merely moves the “your/you” mismatch unless the original intentionally had one of each. More likely, “Vouchsafe you” is a textual variant/typo/red herring, while the true structural break is the displaced envoi line at 25. The 25–26 grammar point is not absolutely decisive because “our music” could be read as a loose antecedent, but combined with the envoi completion it strongly favors **25/74**.

Other proposed pairs, such as 28/74 or 25/68, fail because they do not supply the required *forests/music* pairing in the envoi or disrupt surrounding form/context.

I remain with **25 and 74**; confidence high.
}

